[I] POSIX Shell Compatible Argument Parser

[T] c-shquote is a standalone implementation of POSIX shell compatible
[T] argument quoting and parsing written in ISO C11. It splits command lines
[T] into arguments and quotes strings the way a POSIX shell does, and is
[T] part of the c-util project used by dbus-broker.

[U] https://github.com/c-util/c-shquote

[A] C-shquote Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

